.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tine-delete 1  "delete " 
.SH NAME
tine\-delete \- Delete a block with its children; refuses broken references without \-\-yes and prints the removed text (up to 65,536 UTF\-8 bytes, with omitted byte count)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtine delete\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-graph\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-rev\fR] [\fB\-\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-author\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIBLOCK\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a block with its children; refuses broken references without \-\-yes and prints the removed text (up to 65,536 UTF\-8 bytes, with omitted byte count)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm deletion even when it breaks incoming block references
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable diagnostic logging for the desktop app
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-graph\fR \fI<GRAPH>\fR
The graph. Defaults to $TINE_GRAPH, else the graph folder around the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the typed result (schema tine.cli/1) as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-rev\fR \fI<REV>\fR
Write only if the page is still at this rev (as `page show` prints it); required for a bare PAGE/POS without a fingerprint
.TP
\fB\-\-run\fR \fI<RUN>\fR
Commit this write to the graph\*(Aqs git repository as part of RUN (from `tine run begin`)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTINE_RUN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-author\fR \fI<AUTHOR>\fR
Author on created blocks and on the run\*(Aqs commits (default: TINE_AUTHOR, else agent; blank environment values count as unset). With `edit`, the flag (not the variable) also sets the block\*(Aqs tine.author::
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIBLOCK\fR>

